":"NOASSERTION","url":null,"node_id":"MDc6TGljZW5zZTA="},"allow_forking":true,"is_template":false,"web_commit_signoff_required":false,"topics":["linter","python","typechecker","types","typing"],"visibility":"public","forks":3065,"open_issues":3124,"watchers":20064,"default_branch":"master","permissions":{"admin":false,"maintain":false,"push":false,"triage":false,"pull":true}},"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/pulls/9629","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/9629","diff_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/9629.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/9629.patch","merged_at":"2021-08-26T20:36:42Z"},"body":"### Description\r\n\r\nCloses #5580\r\nPreviously, the type of empty dicts are inferred as `dict[<nothing>, <nothing>]`, which is not a subtype of `Mapping[str, Any]`, and this has caused a false-positive error saying `Keywords must be strings`. This PR fixes it by inferring the types of double-starred arguments with a context of `Mapping[str, Any]`. \r\n\r\nCloses #4001 and closes #9007 (duplicate)\r\nDo not check for \"too many arguments\" error when there are any double-starred arguments. This will lead to some false-negavites, see my comment here: https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/4001#issuecomment-714628193\r\n\r\n### Test Plan\r\n\r\nAdded a simple test `testPassingEmptyDictWithStars`. This single test can cover both of the issues above.\r\n\r\nI also modified some existing tests that were added in #9573 and #6213.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/9629/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":3,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/9629/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}},"event":"cross-referenced"},{"id":5215187475,"node_id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NTIxNTE4NzQ3NQ==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/events/5215187475","actor":{